1 REM FBCS FIL-0204
2 REM CLAIM A-11.2.4.1-04
3 REM TYPE OUTPUT
4 REM STD 11.2.4.1 l.7240-7242: if the most recent operation was a WRITE or
5 REM PRINT, SAME sets the pointer to the FIRST file element created by that
6 REM operation. In SEQUENTIAL a WRITE creates one record; in STREAM each value
7 REM is a file element.
10 OPEN #1: NAME "FIL0204.DAT", ACCESS OUTIN, ORGANIZATION SEQUENTIAL, RECTYPE INTERNAL
20 WRITE #1: 1
30 WRITE #1: 2
40 READ #1, SAME: X
50 PRINT X
60 SET #1: POINTER SAME
70 READ #1: Y
80 PRINT Y
90 CLOSE #1
100 OPEN #2: NAME "FIL0204B.DAT", ACCESS OUTIN, ORGANIZATION STREAM, RECTYPE INTERNAL
110 WRITE #2: 1, 2
120 READ #2, SAME: Z
130 PRINT Z
140 CLOSE #2
150 OPEN #3: NAME "FIL0204C.DAT", ACCESS OUTIN, ORGANIZATION SEQUENTIAL, RECTYPE INTERNAL
160 WRITE #3: 1, 2
170 READ #3, SAME: A, B
180 PRINT A; B
190 CLOSE #3
200 END
